window.CET6_DATA("data/articles/day-070.json",{"day":70,"title":"Planning for the Flood That Has Not Happened","targetWords":[{"word":"abstract","gloss":"抽象的","context":"Every investment was tested against an abstract promise of resilience and a concrete estimate of benefit.","contextParagraph":4,"collocation":null},{"word":"impulse","gloss":"冲动","context":"The town needed a clear objective, not simply the impulse to reproduce the buildings that had stood there before.","contextParagraph":0,"collocation":null},{"word":"mode","gloss":"模式","context":"The essence of the plan was preparation for several possible conditions, with a different operating mode for each.","contextParagraph":3,"collocation":null},{"word":"setback","gloss":"挫折","context":"Residents feared that another storm would turn an ordinary setback into permanent hardship.","contextParagraph":0,"collocation":null},{"word":"scope","gloss":"范围","context":"The scope of support therefore became a question of fairness as well as engineering.","contextParagraph":2,"collocation":null},{"word":"sake","gloss":"目的","context":"For the sake of continued attention, the town published regular progress reports rather than relying on fear.","contextParagraph":4,"collocation":null},{"word":"cue","gloss":"提示","context":"The discrepancy between two water measurements became a cue for further investigation.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"sequence","gloss":"顺序","context":"Although no means could remove every risk, a careful sequence of repairs might improve the odds.","contextParagraph":0,"collocation":null},{"word":"consensus","gloss":"共识","context":"The council eventually reached consensus on temporary protection and long-term reconstruction.","contextParagraph":3,"collocation":null},{"word":"fate","gloss":"命运","context":"The mayor warned against treating fate as an excuse for inaction.","contextParagraph":0,"collocation":null},{"word":"clue","gloss":"线索","context":"Its premise was that rainfall had exceeded the design limit, but one clue suggested another cause: a blocked outlet behind a warehouse.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"stereotype","gloss":"刻板","context":"A stereotype held that waterfront residents were wealthy and could absorb losses, while families elsewhere were described as careless.","contextParagraph":2,"collocation":null},{"word":"criterion","gloss":"标准","context":"The mayor asked the committee to act in accordance with published criteria, so that each applicant would know the criterion used to assess a claim.","contextParagraph":2,"collocation":null},{"word":"essence","gloss":"本质","context":"The essence of the plan was preparation for several possible conditions, with a different operating mode for each.","contextParagraph":3,"collocation":null},{"word":"hardship","gloss":"艰难","context":"Residents feared that another storm would turn an ordinary setback into permanent hardship.","contextParagraph":0,"collocation":null},{"word":"hypothesis","gloss":"假设","context":"An engineer presented a hypothesis about the flooding.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"entity","gloss":"整体","context":"The system treated the town as a connected entity rather than a collection of isolated private properties.","contextParagraph":3,"collocation":null},{"word":"dilemma","gloss":"困境","context":"After a serious flood, a coastal town faced the dilemma of rebuilding quickly or waiting for a safer plan.","contextParagraph":0,"collocation":null},{"word":"incidence","gloss":"发生率","context":"The incidence of damage varied sharply across neighboring streets, making a simple analogy with another town unreliable.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"flaw","gloss":"缺陷","context":"The aftermath brought chaos, left a remnant of mud in every street and exposed a flaw in the old drainage system.","contextParagraph":0,"collocation":null},{"word":"destiny","gloss":"命运","context":"Nor could residents expect perfect security as their destiny.","contextParagraph":3,"collocation":null},{"word":"paradox","gloss":"悖论","context":"The paradox of successful prevention was that its value might never become dramatic news.","contextParagraph":4,"collocation":null},{"word":"shortcoming","gloss":"缺点","context":"The climax of a rescue should not conceal an unresolved shortcoming in prevention.","contextParagraph":3,"collocation":null},{"word":"chaos","gloss":"混乱","context":"The aftermath brought chaos, left a remnant of mud in every street and exposed a flaw in the old drainage system.","contextParagraph":0,"collocation":null},{"word":"premise","gloss":"前提","context":"Its premise was that rainfall had exceeded the design limit, but one clue suggested another cause: a blocked outlet behind a warehouse.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"clarity","gloss":"清楚","context":"The engineer refused to let a persuasive scenario substitute for logic, even when its explanation offered the satisfying clarity residents desperately wanted.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"handicap","gloss":"障碍","context":"One elderly resident described her damaged home without asking for special sympathy; another explained a financial handicap that official forms did not capture.","contextParagraph":2,"collocation":null},{"word":"logic","gloss":"逻辑","context":"The engineer refused to let a persuasive scenario substitute for logic, even when its explanation offered the satisfying clarity residents desperately wanted.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"blur","gloss":"模糊","context":"Both claims could blur the actual plight of people facing expensive repairs.","contextParagraph":2,"collocation":null},{"word":"accordance","gloss":"符合","context":"The mayor asked the committee to act in accordance with published criteria, so that each applicant would know the criterion used to assess a claim.","contextParagraph":2,"collocation":null},{"word":"analogy","gloss":"类比","context":"The incidence of damage varied sharply across neighboring streets, making a simple analogy with another town unreliable.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"drawback","gloss":"缺点","context":"A major drawback was cost, but postponing all decisions would be no solution.","contextParagraph":3,"collocation":null},{"word":"scenario","gloss":"场景","context":"The engineer refused to let a persuasive scenario substitute for logic, even when its explanation offered the satisfying clarity residents desperately wanted.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"facet","gloss":"方面","context":"Each facet of the problem required evidence.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"discrepancy","gloss":"差异","context":"The discrepancy between two water measurements became a cue for further investigation.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"aftermath","gloss":"后果","context":"The aftermath brought chaos, left a remnant of mud in every street and exposed a flaw in the old drainage system.","contextParagraph":0,"collocation":null},{"word":"feat","gloss":"功绩","context":"Emergency barriers represented an impressive feat, yet officials rejected the pretext that this achievement made further investment unnecessary.","contextParagraph":3,"collocation":null},{"word":"sensation","gloss":"轰动","context":"Months later, the initial sensation surrounding the disaster had faded.","contextParagraph":4,"collocation":null},{"word":"stance","gloss":"立场","context":"A responsible public stance combined modest expectations with sustained effort.","contextParagraph":4,"collocation":null},{"word":"plight","gloss":"困境","context":"Both claims could blur the actual plight of people facing expensive repairs.","contextParagraph":2,"collocation":null},{"word":"prototype","gloss":"原型","context":"A prototype drainage model allowed the team to test an alternative configuration.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"pretext","gloss":"借口","context":"Emergency barriers represented an impressive feat, yet officials rejected the pretext that this achievement made further investment unnecessary.","contextParagraph":3,"collocation":null},{"word":"remnant","gloss":"残余","context":"The aftermath brought chaos, left a remnant of mud in every street and exposed a flaw in the old drainage system.","contextParagraph":0,"collocation":null},{"word":"avail","gloss":"用处","context":"Still, waiting for another crisis before acting would be to no avail.","contextParagraph":4,"collocation":null},{"word":"climax","gloss":"高潮","context":"The climax of a rescue should not conceal an unresolved shortcoming in prevention.","contextParagraph":3,"collocation":null},{"word":"configuration","gloss":"构造","context":"A prototype drainage model allowed the team to test an alternative configuration.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"means","gloss":"手段","context":"Although no means could remove every risk, a careful sequence of repairs might improve the odds.","contextParagraph":0,"collocation":null},{"word":"odds","gloss":"可能性","context":"Although no means could remove every risk, a careful sequence of repairs might improve the odds.","contextParagraph":0,"collocation":null},{"word":"and","gloss":"和","context":"The aftermath brought chaos, left a remnant of mud in every street and exposed a flaw in the old drainage system.","contextParagraph":0,"collocation":null},{"word":"for","gloss":"为了","context":"After a serious flood, a coastal town faced the dilemma of rebuilding quickly or waiting for a safer plan.","contextParagraph":0,"collocation":null}],"paragraphs":[{"en":"After a serious flood, a coastal town faced the dilemma of rebuilding quickly or waiting for a safer plan. The aftermath brought chaos, left a remnant of mud in every street and exposed a flaw in the old drainage system. Residents feared that another storm would turn an ordinary setback into permanent hardship. The mayor warned against treating fate as an excuse for inaction. Although no means could remove every risk, a careful sequence of repairs might improve the odds. The town needed a clear objective, not simply the impulse to reproduce the buildings that had stood there before.","zh":"严重洪灾后，沿海小镇面临迅速重建还是等待更安全方案的困境。灾后秩序混乱，每条街都有残泥，旧排水系统缺陷暴露。居民怕下次风暴把普通挫折变成长久艰难。市长提醒别以命运为不行动借口；没有手段能消除所有风险，但仔细安排维修顺序可能提高成功机会。小镇需明确目标，而非冲动复制原建筑。"},{"en":"An engineer presented a hypothesis about the flooding. Its premise was that rainfall had exceeded the design limit, but one clue suggested another cause: a blocked outlet behind a warehouse. The discrepancy between two water measurements became a cue for further investigation. The incidence of damage varied sharply across neighboring streets, making a simple analogy with another town unreliable. A prototype drainage model allowed the team to test an alternative configuration. Each facet of the problem required evidence. The engineer refused to let a persuasive scenario substitute for logic, even when its explanation offered the satisfying clarity residents desperately wanted.","zh":"工程师提出洪水假设，前提是雨量超设计限，但一个线索指向其他原因：仓库后的出水口堵塞。两处水位差异提示深入调查，邻街损害发生率差别巨大，简单类比别的小镇不可靠。排水原型模型让团队测试替代构造。问题每个方面都需证据，工程师不让有说服力的场景推演代替逻辑，即使解释能带来居民急需的清晰感。"},{"en":"Public meetings revealed a different problem. A stereotype held that waterfront residents were wealthy and could absorb losses, while families elsewhere were described as careless. Both claims could blur the actual plight of people facing expensive repairs. One elderly resident described her damaged home without asking for special sympathy; another explained a financial handicap that official forms did not capture. The scope of support therefore became a question of fairness as well as engineering. The mayor asked the committee to act in accordance with published criteria, so that each applicant would know the criterion used to assess a claim.","zh":"公开会议揭示另一问题。刻板印象说滨水居民富有能承受损失，别处家庭粗心，均可能模糊面对昂贵维修者的真实困境。一位老人介绍受损家园而不求特殊同情，另一位说明表格未涵盖的财务障碍。支持范围于是既是工程也是公平问题。市长要求按公布条件行事，使申请者知道评估依据。"},{"en":"The council eventually reached consensus on temporary protection and long-term reconstruction. A major drawback was cost, but postponing all decisions would be no solution. Emergency barriers represented an impressive feat, yet officials rejected the pretext that this achievement made further investment unnecessary. The climax of a rescue should not conceal an unresolved shortcoming in prevention. Nor could residents expect perfect security as their destiny. The essence of the plan was preparation for several possible conditions, with a different operating mode for each. The system treated the town as a connected entity rather than a collection of isolated private properties.","zh":"议会最终就临时保护与长期重建达成共识。主要缺点是成本，但推迟所有决定无助。应急堤坝是杰出成绩，官员却拒绝以此为无需再投资的借口。救援高潮不应掩盖预防不足，人们也不能期待命运带来绝对安全。方案本质是准备多种条件、各配操作模式，把小镇视为相连整体，而非孤立私人地产集合。"},{"en":"Months later, the initial sensation surrounding the disaster had faded. For the sake of continued attention, the town published regular progress reports rather than relying on fear. Every investment was tested against an abstract promise of resilience and a concrete estimate of benefit. The paradox of successful prevention was that its value might never become dramatic news. Still, waiting for another crisis before acting would be to no avail. A responsible public stance combined modest expectations with sustained effort. The town could not command the weather, but it could decide how honestly to understand its vulnerabilities and how deliberately to prepare.","zh":"数月后，灾难最初引起的轰动消退。为保持关注，小镇定期公开进度，不靠恐惧。每项投资既检验抽象韧性承诺，也估算具体收益。成功预防的悖论是其价值可能永不上大新闻，但等新危机才行动毫无用处。负责立场结合适度期待与持续努力。小镇不能指挥天气，却能决定多诚实理解脆弱、多认真准备。"}],"previous":69,"next":71});
